  "dom_id": "step-q7990",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $2{x}^{2}-49{y}^{2}=98?$",
  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-49{y}^{2} & =98 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{98}-\\frac{49{y}^{2}}{98} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we $a=\\sqrt{49}=7$ and $b=\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$",
